<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3508" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρό-ᾱσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hearing, hearkening</i> or <i>listening to</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.21
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ποιεῖσθαί τινος,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκροᾶσθαι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέπτειν τὴν ἀ. ὑμῶν</span>
			to cheat you into <i>hearing</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.35
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>obedience</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐν ἀρχῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>thing listened to, recitation, lecture</i>, <i><span class="en">Hp.
				<u>Praec.</u>,12</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				32.2.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.466
			</span></i>, etc.:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυσικὴ
			ἀ.</span>, title of work by <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκροατήριον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.58c
			</span></i>.</div>
